From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kv-cache <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rocm-aic: install the ionic verbs provider and vllm-router

Without libionic1 the image has ZERO RDMA devices -- ibv_get_device_list()
returns 0 even privileged with /dev/infiniband mounted -- and UCX silently
falls back to TCP, so NIXL "works" while moving no RDMA bytes at all.
vllm-router is upstream's P/D router, which proxy.py cannot substitute for.

The rixl block sets PYTHONPATH explicitly. nixl_rocm is meson-installed into
/opt/nixl/lib/python3/dist-packages, not pip-installed, and the Dockerfile's
ENV PYTHONPATH is set BELOW this block -- so importing it here without that
export fails at build time while succeeding in the finished image.

Carried out-of-tree. See README.md and HANDOFF.md BLOCKER 4.
---
diff --git a/docker/Dockerfile b/docker/Dockerfile
--- a/docker/Dockerfile
+++ b/docker/Dockerfile
@@ -529,6 +529,129 @@
         || { echo "ERROR: hsa-snoop built without Prometheus mode (--prometheus absent)" >&2; exit 1; } && \
     echo "PASS: hsa-snoop v${HSA_SNOOP_REF} with Prometheus exporter (incl. AIS metrics) installed"
 
+# ----- 6c. RDMA userspace provider + P/D router ------------------------------
+# Two pieces the MP-mode P/D architecture needs and the ROCm base image does
+# not carry. Both are cheap; both are load-bearing; one of them fails silently.
+#
+# (1) libionic1 — the AMD/Pensando USERSPACE verbs provider for the `ionic`
+#     RoCE NICs. libibverbs dlopen()s providers listed in /etc/libibverbs.d/,
+#     and Ubuntu's stock rdma-core (50.x in this base) ships mlx5, bnxt_re,
+#     irdma and friends but NOT ionic. Without this package
+#     ibv_get_device_list() returns 0 *inside the container* even though
+#     /dev/infiniband/uverbs* are present and the container is privileged.
+#
+#     That is not a loud failure. UCX simply omits every RDMA transport, and
+#     NIXL / vLLM's NixlConnector fall back to TCP: transfers still complete,
+#     needles still return, nothing errors — the stack just quietly stops being
+#     RDMA, which is the entire premise of MP P/D. See HANDOFF.md BLOCKER 4,
+#     and lab/verify_nixl_rdma.py for the check that catches it.
+#
+#     The .deb is staged into the build context at ainic/ by build.sh from the
+#     lab host's /opt/amd/ainic/deb-repo — a local file:// repo, not something
+#     apt can reach from inside a build. build.sh fails loudly when it is
+#     missing rather than letting a TCP-only image out the door.
+#
+# (2) vllm-router — upstream's P/D router (github.com/vllm-project/router). It
+#     threads the NIXL handshake and stamps ___prefill_addr_…___decode_addr_…
+#     into the request id; proxy.py only forwards HTTP prefill->decode and
+#     cannot substitute for it.
+#
+#     It is a self-contained Rust binary in a manylinux_2_28 wheel and declares
+#     NO dependency on vllm, so it cannot drag a second, non-ROCm vLLM into the
+#     image — only orjson is added. The version is pinned because this is the
+#     component that decides which instance prefills; an unpinned router is a
+#     silent behaviour change in the middle of the measurement.
+ARG VLLM_ROUTER_VERSION=0.1.15
+
+COPY ainic/ /tmp/ainic/
+RUN dpkg -i /tmp/ainic/libionic1_*.deb && \
+    rm -rf /tmp/ainic && \
+    test -e /etc/libibverbs.d/ionic.driver \
+        || { echo "ERROR: ionic.driver absent after installing libionic1" >&2; exit 1; } && \
+    echo "PASS: ionic userspace verbs provider installed"
+
+#     The vLLM check reads installed *metadata* rather than importing vllm.
+#     `import vllm` pulls in torch and dies with "No CUDA GPUs are available"
+#     on any machine without a visible GPU -- which is every docker build. An
+#     import-based guard here does not detect a displaced vLLM, it just fails
+#     the build 100% of the time. Build-time guards must not import
+#     GPU-dependent packages.
+RUN python3 -m pip install --no-cache-dir "vllm-router==${VLLM_ROUTER_VERSION}" && \
+    test -x /usr/local/bin/vllm-router && \
+    vllm-router --help 2>&1 | grep -q -- '--vllm-pd-disaggregation' \
+        || { echo "ERROR: vllm-router lacks --vllm-pd-disaggregation" >&2; exit 1; } && \
+    python3 -c 'import importlib.metadata as m, sys; sys.exit(0 if "rocm" in m.version("vllm") else 1)' \
+        || { echo "ERROR: installing vllm-router displaced the ROCm vLLM" >&2; exit 1; } && \
+    echo "PASS: vllm-router ${VLLM_ROUTER_VERSION} installed, ROCm vLLM intact"
+
+# (3) rixl -- the package name vLLM actually imports on ROCm (BLOCKER 5).
+#     vllm/distributed/nixl_utils.py selects the NIXL python package by platform:
+#
+#         package_name = "rixl" if current_platform.is_rocm() else "nixl"
+#
+#     This NIXL build installs `nixl_rocm` and ships a `nixl` shim for it. It
+#     ships no `rixl` AT ALL, so that import raises ImportError -- which
+#     nixl_utils CATCHES, quietly setting NixlWrapper = None. The only surface
+#     symptom is NixlConnector dying with RuntimeError("NIXL is not available")
+#     on an image where NIXL demonstrably works (lab/verify_nixl_rdma.py moves
+#     64 MiB over it). Baking the shim in is what stops a from-scratch rebuild
+#     from silently regressing to that state -- it lived only as a hand-applied
+#     layer until 2026-09-11.
+#
+#     The guard is import-based but safe: `rixl` pulls in nixl_rocm bindings,
+#     not torch, so it does not need a GPU and will not fail every build the
+#     way `import vllm` would.
+#
+#     This block must set PYTHONPATH itself, and must NOT import nixl_rocm.
+#     Both follow from one fact: /opt/nixl is wired into the environment by the
+#     `ENV` block ~35 lines BELOW here, so at THIS layer neither PYTHONPATH nor
+#     LD_LIBRARY_PATH points into it yet.
+#       - nixl_rocm is MESON-installed to /opt/nixl/lib/python3/dist-packages
+#         and is NOT a pip package (`pip list` shows nothing for it), so
+#         without the export below the probe is a ModuleNotFoundError.
+#       - actually importing it then ALSO needs libnixl.so from
+#         /opt/nixl/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu, equally absent from the loader path
+#         until that ENV -- so an import-based probe still dies with
+#         "libnixl.so: cannot open shared object file" even once PYTHONPATH
+#         is correct. build-nixl.sh exports both, but only into its own
+#         process, which does not outlive its RUN layer.
+#     So the site dir is derived with find_spec(), which LOCATES the package
+#     without executing it or dlopen'ing its extension module. That is the same
+#     rule the vllm-router guard above already states: a build-time guard must
+#     not import.
+#
+#     Both failures were observed on the first real from-scratch rebuild
+#     (2026-09-12, stage 36/37). The image was always correct at RUNTIME, which
+#     is exactly why hand-testing this shim inside a finished container passed
+#     while the build it is supposed to reproduce did not.
+RUN export PYTHONPATH="/opt/nixl/lib/python3/dist-packages:${PYTHONPATH:-}" && \
+    NIXL_PY=$(python3 -c 'import importlib.util as u, os; s = u.find_spec("nixl_rocm"); print(os.path.dirname(s.submodule_search_locations[0]))') \
+        || { echo "ERROR: cannot locate nixl_rocm under /opt/nixl -- did the meson install move?" >&2; exit 1; } && \
+    mkdir -p "${NIXL_PY}/rixl" && \
+    printf '%s\n' \
+'"""ROCm shim: vLLM imports rixl on ROCm; this NIXL build installs nixl_rocm.' \
+'' \
+'Mirrors nixl/__init__.py, registering the same submodules under rixl.*.' \
+'Keep the two in sync: they are the same shim twice. See patches/0012.' \
+'"""' \
+'' \
+'import importlib' \
+'import sys' \
+'' \
+'_pkg = importlib.import_module("nixl_rocm")' \
+'' \
+'for sub_name in ("_api", "_bindings", "_utils", "logging"):' \
+'    module = importlib.import_module(f"{_pkg.__name__}.{sub_name}")' \
+'    sys.modules[f"rixl.{sub_name}"] = module' \
+'    setattr(sys.modules[__name__], sub_name, module)' \
+'    for attr in dir(module):' \
+'        if not attr.startswith("_"):' \
+'            setattr(sys.modules[__name__], attr, getattr(module, attr))' \
+      > "${NIXL_PY}/rixl/__init__.py" && \
+    python3 -c 'import importlib.util as u, sys; sys.exit(0 if u.find_spec("rixl") else 1)' \
+        || { echo "ERROR: rixl shim not importable after install" >&2; exit 1; } && \
+    echo "PASS: rixl shim installed at ${NIXL_PY}/rixl"
+
 # ----- 7. Runtime environment ------------------------------------------------
 # Vars from upstream vLLM Dockerfile.rocm added here:
 #   HSA_ENABLE_IPC_MODE_LEGACY=1  — legacy HIP IPC for cross-container KV registration (LMCache MP)
